-- `exp` in the math library is `EXPONENT EULER x`, so it inherits the error when
-- the result is too large. Its result is a plain NUMBER, not a MAYBE.
-- The digits of e to the power 709 come from the platform's floating-point
-- library and differ between platforms, so this file checks that the answer
-- lies between two powers of 2, both exact on every platform, and never
-- prints it.

IMPORT math

#EVAL exp 709 > EXPONENT 2 1022 AND exp 709 < EXPONENT 2 1023
#EVAL exp 710
